.Dd $Mdocdate: August 1 2026 $
.Dt XSUNABA 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm Xsunaba
.Nd sandbox X11 applications with Xephyr, pledge, and unveil
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar command Op Ar argument ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility provides a two-layer sandbox for running X11 GUI applications
on OpenBSD:
.Bl -enum -compact -offset indent
.It
Display isolation via a nested
.Xr Xephyr 1
X server, which prevents the application from reading
.Xr XEvents 3
(keystrokes, mouse input, clipboard) intended for other windows in the
parent X session.
.It
Process restriction via
.Xr pledge 2
and
.Xr unveil 2 ,
which limit the system calls and filesystem access available to the
application process.
Both are configured through environment variables.
.El
.Pp
When invoked from the command line,
.Nm
starts Xephyr on an unused display (default
.Ql :32
\-
.Ql :99 ) ,
generates an X11 magic cookie for authentication, forks the target
application with user-specified pledge and unveil restrictions, waits
for it to exit, then stops Xephyr and cleans up the authentication
cookie.
.Pp
.Nm
can also be loaded as a Perl module via
.Cm require
to incorporate pledge/unveil functionality into custom scripts,
either with or without the Xephyr display layer.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "XSUNABA_UNVEIL"
.It Ev XSUNABA_PLEDGE
Space-separated list of pledge promises applied to the sandboxed
application immediately before
.Xr exec 3 .
.Pp
Default:
.Ql stdio rpath wpath cpath fattr proc exec inet dns unix tty .
.Pp
Set to an empty string to disable pledge for the application.
See
.Xr pledge 2
for the full set of available promises.
.It Ev XSUNABA_UNVEIL
Comma-separated list of
.Ar path : Ar perm
entries passed to
.Xr unveil 2
for the sandboxed application.
.Pp
When unset, the application inherits the launcher's filesystem view
and no additional unveil restrictions are applied (the filesystem is
fully visible).
When set, only the listed paths are accessible after unveil is locked;
all other paths become invisible.
.Pp
Permission codes are single-letter abbreviations that may be combined:
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width "rwxc" -compact -offset indent
.It r
Read files, list directories.
.It rx
Read and execute.
.It rw
Read and write existing files.
.It rwx
Read, write, and execute existing files.
.It rwc
Read, write, and create new files.
.It rwxc
Read, write, execute, and create (full access).
.El
.Pp
Example:
.Ql /usr/X11R6/bin/xterm:rx,/tmp:rwc,/etc:r,/dev:r .
.Pp
The
.Pa /tmp/.X11-unix
socket directory and
.Pa /dev
are always unveiled for the application with
.Ql rwc
and
.Ql r
respectively, so they do not need to be listed unless you wish to
change their permissions.
.It Ev XSUNABA_DISPLAY
Starting X display number for
.Xr Xephyr 1 .
If the socket
.Pa /tmp/.X11-unix/X Ns Ao Ar N Ac
already exists,
.Nm
scans upward from this number to find a free display.
Default:
.Ql :32 .
.It Ev WIDTH
.Xr Xephyr 1
display width in pixels.
Default:
.Ql 1024 .
.It Ev HEIGHT
.Xr Xephyr 1
display height in pixels.
Default:
.Ql 768 .
.It Ev VERBOSE
When set to any true value, emits diagnostic messages to standard
error during setup, application launch, and cleanup.
Each message is prefixed with
.Ql [Xsunaba] .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "$HOME/.Xauthority-xsunaba"
.It Pa $HOME/.Xauthority-xsunaba
Temporary X authority file created for the Xephyr session.
Contains the magic cookie used to authenticate the application
connection.
Removed during cleanup.
.It Pa /tmp/.X11-unix/
Directory scanned for existing X11 sockets to find a free display
number.
.It Pa /usr/bin/openssl
Used to generate the X11 magic cookie (128-bit random hex string).
.It Pa /usr/X11R6/bin/xauth
Used to add and remove X11 authentication cookies.
.It Pa /usr/X11R6/bin/Xephyr
The nested X server executable.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Pp
If no command is provided, the usage message is printed to standard
error and the exit status is 255.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Launch Firefox with filesystem restrictions and a tighter pledge:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ XSUNABA_UNVEIL="/usr/X11R6/bin/firefox:rx,/tmp:rwc,/etc:r" \e
  XSUNABA_PLEDGE="stdio rpath wpath cpath proc exec inet dns unix tty" \e
  Xsunaba firefox --private-window
.Ed
.Pp
Run xterm with minimal access, verbose output enabled:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ VERBOSE=1 \e
  XSUNABA_UNVEIL="/usr/X11R6/bin/xterm:rx,/tmp:rwc,/etc:r" \e
  Xsunaba xterm
.Ed
.Pp
Use Xsunaba as a Perl module for a custom launcher (no Xephyr):
.Bd -literal -offset indent
#!/usr/bin/perl
require '/usr/local/bin/Xsunaba';

Xsunaba::sandbox(
    app    => 'xterm',
    unveil => [
        '/usr/X11R6/bin/xterm:rx',
        '/tmp:rwc',
        '/etc:r',
    ],
    pledge => 'stdio rpath wpath cpath inet dns unix tty',
);
.Ed
.Pp
Use the low-level API for maximum control:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
#!/usr/bin/perl
require '/usr/local/bin/Xsunaba';

Xsunaba::unveil('/usr/X11R6/bin/firefox',  'rx');
Xsunaba::unveil("$ENV{HOME}/.mozilla",     'rwc');
Xsunaba::unveil('/tmp',                     'rwc');
Xsunaba::unveil('/etc',                     'r');
Xsunaba::unveil('/usr/local/lib',           'rx');
Xsunaba::unveil('/usr/lib',                 'rx');
Xsunaba::unveil_lock();
Xsunaba::pledge('stdio rpath wpath cpath proc exec inet dns unix tty');

exec 'firefox', '--private-window' or die "exec: $!";
.Ed
.Pp
Override the default pledge promises:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
#!/usr/bin/perl
require '/usr/local/bin/Xsunaba';
$Xsunaba::PLEGE_PROMISES = 'stdio rpath inet dns';
Xsunaba::sandbox(app => 'curl', args => ['-O', 'https://example.com']);
.Ed
.Pp
Launch a sandbox on a custom display with custom geometry:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ XSUNABA_DISPLAY=":40" WIDTH=1280 HEIGHT=900 Xsunaba gimp
.Ed
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
Set
.Ev VERBOSE
to any true value to see diagnostic messages on standard error:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[INFO] using display :32
[INFO] Xephyr started (PID 12345)
[INFO] launched 'firefox' (PID 12346)
[INFO] stopping Xephyr (PID 12345)
[INFO] cleanup complete
.Ed
.Pp
Warnings (always printed) indicate non-fatal issues such as a failed
pledge call on a non-OpenBSD system.
Errors (always printed) indicate fatal conditions such as
.Ev HOME
not being set or Xephyr failing to start.
.Sh MODULE API
.Nm
may be loaded as a Perl module using
.Cm require :
.Pp
.Dl require '/usr/local/bin/Xsunaba';
.Pp
The following functions are exported into the
.Sy Xsunaba
namespace:
.Bl -tag -width "unveil_lock()"
.It Fn pledge $promises
Invoke
.Xr pledge 2
with the given space-separated promise string.
If
.Ar $promises
is
.Dv undef
or omitted, the package variable
.Va $Xsunaba::PLEGE_PROMISES
is used as the default.
No-op on systems other than OpenBSD.
.It Fn unveil $path $perm
Invoke
.Xr unveil 2
for
.Ar $path
with permission
.Ar $perm
(default
.Ql r ) .
Must be called before
.Fn unveil_lock .
No-op on systems other than OpenBSD, or if unveil is already locked.
.It Fn unveil_lock
Lock the unveil configuration by calling
.Fn unveil
with two
.Dv NULL
arguments.
After this call, the filesystem is restricted to the set of paths
announced with
.Fn unveil ,
and no further unveil calls are permitted.
No-op on systems other than OpenBSD.
.It Fn sandbox %opts
Convenience wrapper that applies unveil and pledge, then
.Xr exec 3 Ns s
the application directly (no
.Xr Xephyr 1 ) .
Accepts the following keys:
.Bl -tag -width "unveil" -compact -offset indent
.It Cm app
Executable to run (required).
.It Cm args
Array reference of command-line arguments.
.It Cm pledge
Promise string (defaults to
.Va $Xsunaba::PLEGE_PROMISES ) .
.It Cm unveil
Array reference of
.Ql path:perm
strings.
.It Cm lock
Boolean controlling whether
.Fn unveil_lock
is called automatically.
Defaults to true when
.Cm unveil
entries exist.
.El
.It Fn launch %opts
Full sandbox launcher: starts
.Xr Xephyr 1 ,
forks the application with pledge and unveil, waits for the
application to exit, then stops Xephyr and removes the X11
authentication cookie.
Accepts the following keys:
.Bl -tag -width "display" -compact -offset indent
.It Cm app
Executable to run (required).
.It Cm args
Array reference of command-line arguments.
.It Cm display
X display number (default
.Ql :32 ) .
.It Cm width
Xephyr width in pixels (default
.Ql 1024 ) .
.It Cm height
Xephyr height in pixels (default
.Ql 768 ) .
.It Cm pledge
Promise string for the application.
.It Cm unveil
Array reference of
.Ql path:perm
strings.
.El
.El
.Ss Package variables
.Bl -tag -width "PLEGE_PROMISES"
.It Va $Xsunaba::PLEGE_PROMISES
Default pledge promise string used by
.Fn pledge ,
.Fn sandbox ,
and
.Fn launch
when no explicit promise string is provided.
Default:
.Ql stdio rpath wpath cpath fattr proc exec inet dns unix tty .
Set this variable before calling any sandbox function to override the
default for the entire script.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr openssl 1 ,
.Xr perl 1 ,
.Xr xauth 1 ,
.Xr Xephyr 1 ,
